<title>BELGIUM: VW /Audi seek hearing on car pricing probe.</title>
<headline>VW /Audi seek hearing on car pricing probe.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German car manufacturer Volkswagen and its subsidiary Audi have sought a European Commission hearing into allegations of distribution restrictions on the Italian market, an EU source told reporters.</p>
<p>The source, who asked not to be named, said the two carmakers had replied to Commission requests for information related to complaints that their Italian distributors had refused to sell to Austrian, German and French customers.</p>
<p>In supplying information, which is under scrutiny by the Commission, the parties sought a hearing on the case which the source said was likely to take place &quot;some time in April&quot;.</p>
<p>Under EU law, which exempts car distribution from competition rules, carmakers may conclude exclusive dealership arrangements for their vehicles as long as customers are allowed to buy the car of their choice wherever it is cheapest.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 (PIC)</p>
</text>
